# novacore-server

Runnable application host for Novacore Platform. This package is the composition root: it will assemble the inbound FastAPI adapter, Runtime services, and infrastructure/provider adapters.

## Phase 40 scope

This phase establishes only the server package, environment configuration, FastAPI application factory, ASGI entry point, and local startup command. It intentionally does not initialize Firestore or Google ADK and does not register business API routes. Those responsibilities are added in the next phases after the composition contracts are wired.

## Install and run

From the repository root:

```bash
python -m pip install -e 'apps/novacore-server[server]'
cp apps/novacore-server/.env.example apps/novacore-server/.env
novacore-server
```

Alternatively:

```bash
uvicorn novacore_server.main:app --app-dir apps/novacore-server/src --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000 --reload
```

If installed editable, the module can also be started with:

```bash
uvicorn novacore_server.main:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000 --reload
```

The OpenAPI document is available at `http://127.0.0.1:8000/openapi.json`. No health or business endpoints are introduced in Phase 40.

## Configuration

| Variable | Default | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `NOVACORE_APP_NAME` | `Novacore Platform` | OpenAPI application title |
| `NOVACORE_ENVIRONMENT` | `development` | Environment name; development enables CLI reload |
| `NOVACORE_HOST` | `127.0.0.1` | Bind address |
| `NOVACORE_PORT` | `8000` | Bind port |
| `NOVACORE_LOG_LEVEL` | `info` | Uvicorn log level |
| `NOVACORE_CORS_ORIGINS` | empty | Comma-separated allowed browser origins |

The server reads environment variables directly. The example `.env` file is documentation/template only; loading `.env` files is deliberately left to the deployment environment or shell in this phase.

## Architecture boundary

`novacore-server` is an application host, not a new Kernel or Runtime layer. It may depend on adapter packages and Runtime in later phases. Kernel and Runtime remain independent of FastAPI and infrastructure SDKs.

# Novacore Server

Runnable FastAPI host and composition root for Novacore Platform. The server
constructs infrastructure adapters and injects them into Runtime services;
Kernel and Runtime remain independent of FastAPI, Firestore SDK, and Google ADK.

## Install from the repository root

```bash
python -m pip install -e packages/novacore-foundation
python -m pip install -e packages/novacore-kernel
python -m pip install -e packages/novacore-runtime
python -m pip install -e 'packages/novacore-fastapi[fastapi]'
python -m pip install -e 'packages/novacore-firestore[firestore]'
python -m pip install -e 'packages/novacore-google-adk[google-adk]'
python -m pip install -e 'apps/novacore-server[server]'
```

Install only the packages that exist in your checkout; `novacore-foundation`
is listed separately because it is part of the agreed package layout.

## Configure

Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and export its values in your shell (or use your
preferred environment loader). For the Firestore Emulator:

```bash
export FIRESTORE_EMULATOR_HOST=127.0.0.1:8089
export GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT=novacore-local
```

Google ADK execution is opt-in until the host supplies its actual agent. Set
`NOVACORE_ADK_AGENT_FACTORY=your_package.module:build_agent`; the callable
receives `ServerSettings` and must return a configured Google ADK Agent.

## Run

```bash
novacore-server
```

The server listens at `http://127.0.0.1:8000`. Phase 42 registers the HTTP
routers. This phase constructs the shared Firestore stores, HumanReviewService,
and (when configured) GoogleADKAgentExecutor and AgentRevisionExecutionPort.

## Important integration boundary

The host must still provide authentication/authorization, revision-source
authorization, execution-input loading, review-context loading, and revision
history loading. These are application-specific policies and data sources;
the server does not invent them. Revision orchestration service registration is
blocked until the missing Runtime `services/revision_workflow.py` implementation
is restored in the repository.

